---
// AtlasIT AWS IAM Automation Demo Page
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="AWS IAM Automation Demo">
  <section class="max-w-2xl mx-auto py-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">AWS IAM Automation Demo</h1>
    <p class="mb-6 text-slate-300">
      This page demonstrates automated AWS IAM user, role, and permission management using Terraform, with Okta as the central Identity Provider (IdP). The backend is not fully wired, but you can view the example code, configuration, and outputs below. Use this as a reference for interviews or demos. For a full cross-system workflow (AWS, Entra ID, AD), see <code>IAM_AUTOMATION_OVERVIEW.md</code> in the demo directory.
    </p>
    <div class="bg-slate-800/60 border border-slate-700 rounded-lg p-6 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Terraform Example</h2>
      <pre class="overflow-x-auto text-xs bg-slate-900 p-4 rounded"><code>{`
provider "aws" {
  region     = var.aws_region
  access_key = var.aws_access_key
  secret_key = var.aws_secret_key
}

resource "aws_iam_user" "demo_user" {
  name = var.demo_user_name
}

data "aws_iam_policy_document" "assume_role_policy" {
  statement {
    actions = ["sts:AssumeRole"]
    principals {
      type        = "AWS"
      identifiers = [aws_iam_user.demo_user.arn]
    }
  }
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "demo_role" {
  name               = var.demo_role_name
  assume_role_policy = data.aws_iam_policy_document.assume_role_policy.json
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "attach_policy" {
  role       = aws_iam_role.demo_role.name
  policy_arn = "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AdministratorAccess"
}

output "user_arn" {
  value = aws_iam_user.demo_user.arn
}

output "role_arn" {
  value = aws_iam_role.demo_role.arn
}
`}</code></pre>
      <p class="mt-4 text-slate-400 text-sm">
        See <code>atlasit/terraform/aws-iam-demo/</code> for the full working example and setup instructions.<br />
        For a cohesive Okta-driven IAM automation plan across AWS, Microsoft Entra ID, and Active Directory, see <code>IAM_AUTOMATION_OVERVIEW.md</code> in the same directory.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="bg-slate-800/60 border border-slate-700 rounded-lg p-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">How to Use</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal list-inside text-slate-300 mb-4">
        <li>Copy <code>.env.example</code> to <code>.env</code> and fill in your AWS credentials.</li>
        <li>Export your credentials in your shell.</li>
        <li>Run <code>terraform init</code> and <code>terraform apply</code> in <code>atlasit/terraform/aws-iam-demo/</code>.</li>
        <li>Observe the output ARNs for the created user and role.</li>
        <li>Use <code>terraform destroy</code> to clean up.</li>
        <li>For Okta-driven automation across AWS, Entra ID, and AD, see the <code>IAM_AUTOMATION_OVERVIEW.md</code> for workflow and integration details.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-xs">
        This is a demo. For production, use secure secrets management and follow AWS best practices.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
